import ../../../ui/source_language.dl

to get [source diagnostic reply for] {string:uri} [containing] {a pointer to JSON value:diagnostics}:
    return a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "method" is "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", JSON child "params" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is uri, JSON child "diagnostics" is diagnostics])]]

set main to a UI source document named "main.dl" at "file:///workspace/main.dl" prefixed by "" containing "import helper.dl" using UI CPU analysis
set helper to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at "file:///workspace/helper.dl" containing "helper means: 7" in (main's project)
set other to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at (helper's uri) prefixed by "" containing "unrelated" using UI CPU analysis
set client to a UI language client rooted at "file:///workspace"
set client's project to main's project
set client's project context to main's project's context
set client's model to the UI language model for main in client
set client's opened to true
set client's context to main's context
set client's revision to main's revision
set client's project revision to main's project's revision
begin UI source reports for (main's project)

# A main-file compile reports problems in any loaded source of that project.
set response to source diagnostic reply for (helper's uri) containing (a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "message" is "Imported problem"]])
receive UI language diagnostics response in client
free response
set response to source diagnostic reply for "file:///workspace/pending.dl" containing (a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "message" is "Not viewed yet"]])
receive UI language diagnostics response in client
free response
finish UI source reports for (main's project)
require condition ((helper's diagnostics' length = 1) and ((the JSON text named "message" in (the JSON value at index 0 in (helper's diagnostics))) = "Imported problem")) reporting "Diagnostics for a loaded import were discarded while analyzing its main file."
require condition ((helper's diagnostic revision = helper's revision) and (helper's diagnostic project revision = main's project's revision)) reporting "Imported diagnostics did not retain their project snapshot."
set generation to helper's diagnostic generation
retain UI source diagnostics (helper's diagnostics) at (helper's uri) in (helper's project)
require condition (helper's diagnostic generation = generation) reporting "An identical diagnostic report invalidated its retained presentation."
require condition ((other's diagnostics' length = 0) and (other's diagnostic revision = 0)) reporting "An imported diagnostic escaped into another project's identical URI."
set pending to a UI source document named "pending.dl" at "file:///workspace/pending.dl" containing "not viewed yet" in (main's project)
require condition ((pending's diagnostics' length = 1) and (pending's diagnostic project revision = main's project's revision)) reporting "Opening a source lost the project report received before its view existed."

# Imported analysis can also publish an empty report for the main file.
set client's model to the UI language model for helper in client
set client's opened to true
set client's context to helper's context
set client's revision to helper's revision
set client's project revision to helper's project's revision
set response to source diagnostic reply for (main's uri) containing (a new JSON-RPC array)
receive UI language diagnostics response in client
free response
require condition ((main's diagnostic revision = main's revision) and (main's diagnostic project revision = main's project's revision)) reporting "An empty main-file report was lost while viewing an import."

# Stale project replies and server clearing on close preserve retained reports.
edit UI source document main to (the string form of "import helper.dl\nchanged") at 1.0 seconds
set response to source diagnostic reply for (helper's uri) containing (a new JSON-RPC array)
receive UI language diagnostics response in client
require condition (helper's diagnostics' length = 1) reporting "A preceding project revision erased retained diagnostics."
set client's project revision to main's project's revision
set client's opened to false
receive UI language diagnostics response in client
free response
require condition (helper's diagnostics' length = 1) reporting "Closing an imported model erased its diagnostics."

# A full clean analysis commits empty reports even for imports the server never
# named in its new notification batch. Old cached problems must disappear.
begin UI source reports for (main's project)
finish UI source reports for (main's project)
require condition ((helper's diagnostics' length = 0) and (pending's diagnostics' length = 0)) reporting "A clean project analysis retained problems from an earlier snapshot."
require condition ((helper's diagnostic revision = helper's revision) and (helper's diagnostic project revision = main's project's revision)) reporting "A clean imported source stayed indefinitely in the analyzing state."

free UI language client client
free UI source project (main's project)
free UI source project (other's project)
print line "Diagnostics follow document URIs within their project and retain their analysis snapshots."
